      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Level is 4.4%; momentum is mixed because April's rise reversed partly in May; the May waiting-to-start-job backlog unwind is a potentially one-off downward effect; and the policy mechanism from a 4.35% cash rate creates gradual upward pressure through softer labour demand rather than a sharp immediate jump."
      },
